 "description": "Logic gates: a 4-bit prime-number detector. F(A,B,C,D) = 1 when the number ABCD (A the MSB) is 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 or 13.\nMinterms: F = m(2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13). Minimal sum of products (Karnaugh map): F = A'B'C + A'BD + BC'D + B'CD.\nLeft: NOT (INV), AND and OR gates, a two-level AND-OR circuit -> prime_sop (LED LD0).\nRight: the same function with NAND gates only (NAND-NAND; each NOT is a NAND with its inputs tied together) -> prime_nand (LED LD1).\nBoard: the switches SW3..SW0 are A..D (sw(3) = A ... sw(0) = D); LD0 and LD1 light for a prime. Both outputs always agree.",
 "generatedFile": "src/gates.vhd"
}
